## Architecture Rules

### 4 microservices — ports
- policy-service: 8001 (customers + policies)
- claims-service: 8002 (claims lifecycle)
- notification-service: 8003 (async emails via Celery)
- audit-service: 8004 (immutable event log)

### Communication
- Async by default: Kafka topics `policy.*` and `claim.*`
- Sync (only one case): HTTP claims-service → policy-service to verify policy is ACTIVE before creating a claim
- Never share databases between services
- Never add new inter-service HTTP calls — use Kafka

### Internal service structure
```
apps/
├── core/           # health, exceptions, pagination, middleware
└── [domain]/
    ├── models.py      # ORM only, zero business logic
    ├── serializers.py # DRF request/response schemas
    ├── views.py       # Thin ViewSets — HTTP only, call service
    ├── services.py    # ALL business logic lives here
    ├── events.py      # Kafka producers
    ├── consumers.py   # Kafka consumers
    ├── tasks.py       # Celery tasks (notification-service only)
    ├── clients.py     # HTTP client to other services (claims only)
    └── tests/
```

